cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this protocol or the accompanying code, please use the metadata below."
title: "A powered null on a verified channel: separating effect-absent from low power in embodied LLM agents"
# This abstract must match the Abstract section of manuscript/main.md verbatim.
# analysis/scripts/check_claim_boundary.py compares them on every run, so editing
# one without the other fails repro.sh.
abstract: >-
  An exponential moving average over an embodied language-model agent's recent
  movement modulates the temperature used for its next generation. A completed
  forensic study establishes that this channel is causal, is separable from the
  static location channel, and vanishes without residue under ablation, while a
  positive control shows that the same estimator can return zero. A completed
  measurement on a single model then found no shift in a five-way zone decision
  exceeding the materiality margin fixed in advance: a mean total-variation
  distance of 0.038065 against a margin of 0.10, obtained at full nominal power
  over 4,800 draws. This Stage 1 protocol estimates the same quantity in a second model
  family, with a control arm that re-runs the original model to absorb a backend
  version change. Thresholds, decision rules and outcome-neutral checks are fixed
  before any prospective draw exists, and no directional expectation is stated.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Miura"
    given-names: "Mikoto"
    alias: "mikotomiura"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4196-0508"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
# `license` mirrors the LICENSE files actually shipped in this repository.
#   Code (analysis/)         = Apache-2.0 OR MIT -> LICENSE / LICENSE-MIT
#   Manuscript (manuscript/) = CC-BY-4.0         -> LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt
# CFF can only express a list of SPDX identifiers, not a per-part mapping.
# The exact mapping is in README.md, under Licence.
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mikotomiura/powered-null"
version: "0.1.0-stage1"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
# doi: to be filled in once a DOI is minted. The key is omitted until then, because an
#      empty value would be rendered as-is by the GitHub citation widget.
# preferred-citation: to point at the peer-reviewed version once it exists. Omitted
#      until then, for the same reason.
keywords:
  - measurement validity
  - LLM agents
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
  - registered report
  - equivalence margin
